  "summary": "Bumps the minimum supported Clang compiler version from 17.0 to 19.0 across CMake checks, CI environments, and documentation. It replaces the CMake check for aggregate CTAD with a check for C++20 CTAD on alias templates, configures clang-format to use the latest standard, and removes an obsolete libc++ workaround in fuzz testing.",
  "problem": "Supporting Clang versions below 19 blocks the use of C++20 Class Template Argument Deduction (CTAD) for alias templates and necessitates maintaining legacy compiler workarounds in the codebase.",
